message: "If you use or refer to SILT Core v0.2, please cite this release. Licensing is split by artefact type; see LICENSING.md."
title: "SILT Core v0.2: Semantic Architecture for Plural Encounters"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fakhry"
    given-names: "Gareth"
version: "0.2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sugarlicks/silt-identity-core"
url: "https://github.com/Sugarlicks/silt-identity-core"
abstract: >-
  SILT Core v0.2 defines a semantic architecture for encounters between
  participants operating under different legal, customary, cultural, private,
  institutional or technical orders. Its canonical seam is Source → Standing →
  Presentation → evaluation at the encounter. SILT is designed to support mutual
  legibility without requiring originating orders to collapse into a single
  ontology or surrender their own sources of authority.
keywords:
  - "semantic interoperability"
  - "plural legal orders"
  - "customary law"
  - "Indigenous governance"
  - "standing"
  - "authority"
  - "private ordering"
  - "AI agents"
  - "digital infrastructure"
